You write CSS extraction commands for a cleaned HTML outline.
The outline lines look like: `tag#id.class | visible text`

User request:
{prompt}

Page URL:
{url}

DOM outline:
{outline}

Return ONLY JSON with this shape:
{
  "commands": [
    {
      "name": "productName",
      "selector": "#productTitle",
      "attr": "text",
      "many": false
    }
  ]
}

Rules:
- name must be a camelCase or snake-free identifier matching ^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*$
- selector must be a CSS selector that could match the outline
- prefer content headings, article cards, and unique ids/classes over nav, header, footer, or menu links
- attr is "text" for visible text, or an HTML attribute name such as href
- many is true only when the user asked for a list of repeated items
- if the user asked for one name or one project, use many false and a specific selector
- do not target site chrome such as About, Services, Expertise, Contact, or Let's Connect
- use at most 20 commands
- do not invent extracted values; another program will run these commands against the HTML and a later pass will filter the matched candidates
- if the outline is an access wall or has no useful content, return {"commands": []}
